  "question": {
    "text": "Given three points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> lies on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis. If the equation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is parallel to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis, then the centroid of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#916;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> lies on the line&nbsp;"
  },
